[Music]  an out-of-place artifact is  any historical object that seems at a  glance to go against our understanding  of historical chronology  some artifacts appear too advanced for  the technology of the period in which  they were created  and seem almost like they've fallen out  of time the exciting mystery of these  artifacts has led to a range of wild  speculation  involving everything from aliens to time  travel  as much fun as it is to think someone  with a flux capacitor popped by and  accidentally left a  cell phone in ancient rome most of these  objects have reasonable explanations  but the real historical context behind  these out-of-place artifacts and the  ancient cultures which produce them can  be just as interesting as speculative  theories  so let's take a look at seven of the  most thought-provoking and uncover how  such astounding artifacts were created  the anti-ketheria mechanism is an  ancient greek object which has amazed  archaeologists historians and  classicists for decades  the artifact consists of various  incomplete bronze gear fragments which  once formed a kind of primitive machine  sometimes described as the world's first  analog computer  it was discovered in a shipwreck off the  coast of antikytheria island  most archaeologists believe greek  scientists constructed the mechanism  around 87 bc  the technological prowess on display  wouldn't be matched until over a  thousand years later  hence why it seems so out of place in  truth however the greeks around this  period were just that proficient with  complex gear work  with ancient literature describing in  detail the construction of similar  devices  but what did this early machine do based  on recreations  archaeologists think the mechanism was a  sort of astronomical clock able to  predict the position of the moon and  even eclipses decades in advance  likely for the purpose of astrology and  cultural festivals  other devices like astrolabes were also  used in later centuries to make similar  calculations but  none were at the same level as the  anti-ethereum mechanism for quite a  while  making the invention quite impressive  even if it isn't technically out of  place  up next we have the roman dodecahedron  small hollow objects made in the second  to fourth century ce  which looked quite bizarre at a glance  the 12-sided shapes are made of copper  and were spread all over the roman  empire with archaeologists discovering  over a hundred since the 18th century  funnily enough as far as we've been able  to uncover the ancient romans never  bothered to record what the purpose of  these dodecahedrons were  while the lack of explanation lends the  objects a certain mysterious power  truthfully it's more likely the romans  never recorded their  purpose because they were ordinary  enough that everybody already knew what  they were  archaeologists have put forth various  theories regarding their usage  including dice coin measuring and  knitting aids  but in this case the right answer is  probably the most mundane  trace amounts of wax have been found  inside some of the objects suggesting  the dodecahedrons were in fact used  as candle holders the iron pillar of  delhi is a metal structure now located  in delhi india  dating back to the 4th or 5th century ce  at 7.2 meters or roughly  24 feet high and over 3 tons or 6  000 pounds in weight it's an incredible  feat of engineering  any normal iron pillar would have  corroded away long ago  yet the pillar of delhi is famous for  its astonishing resistance to rust  despite being well over a thousand years  old indeed some have claimed the pillar  is completely rust-free  and therefore must be the result of  something beyond the realm of science  any actual photos of the pillar however  make it clear  this isn't the case there unmistakably  is rust on the pillar  even if it's in unbelievable condition  the real secret to the pillar's  longevity lies in the skill of 4th  century indian metallurgists who  constructed the iron pillar through a  complex process  involving rust resistant compounds it's  an inspiring feat of engineering  even if it's not something historians  somehow can't explain  the stone spheres of costa rica are a  collection of over 300 circular rocks  with mysterious origins  the objects are attributed to the  decrees culture an indigenous  civilization of costa rica which  flourished from 700 to 1530 ce  the spheres come in all sizes and have a  certain mystery to them  compounded by the fact their exact  significance remains shrouded in  uncertainty  most popular theories propose they were  placed in lines before the houses of  rulers but we really don't know  regardless of their exact meaning some  have suggested the sphere size  and impressive geometric roundness were  beyond the capabilities of the decreased  culture  frankly this isn't giving the decrees  enough credit the civilization was  highly advanced  producing other forms of impressive  sculptures like the metal effigy you see  currently whatever the cultural purpose  behind the spheres there is no reason to  suspect the dequeues society couldn't  produce them  the main penny is a norwegian silver  coin dating back to the viking age  the coin itself is ordinary enough but  what makes it an  out-of-place artifact is the fact it was  discovered in the state of maine in the  u.s  the coin's existence has been suggested  as evidence a group of vikings made it  all the way to the shores of modern day  north america during their travels when  the coin was first discovered in 1957  the idea of vikings ever crossed the  atlantic ocean was pretty new  but today it's a much more widely  accepted theory thanks to other forms of  evidence coming to light while the coin  itself does appear to be an actual  viking coin  there is still some debate regarding its  authenticity  as it might have been brought over by a  later traveler regardless this is the  one artifact on this list where the far  out explanation isn't actually that far  off and most historians agree is the  correct one  dogu are small statues from the jomon  period of japan with a distinctive  appearance to modern observers the  statues almost resemble a person wearing  a spacesuit  so did an alien or a time traveler  decked out in anachronistic gear  accidentally stumble around ancient  japan long enough to get statues made in  their likeness  maybe but it's far more likely the  resemblance to any modern clothing is  simply coincidental  indeed if these statues are considered  in context with other versions you can  see  most dogu look decidedly far off from  the distinctive spacesuit-like  appearance of the more famous figurines  the majority of dogu effigies from the  surrounding period actually place  emphasis on the wide hips more than  anything else with some lacking heads  altogether  the exaggerated hips and abdomens of  these statues has led historians to  theorize that they were in fact  associated with fertility instead of  spacemen  maybe not as exciting as time travel but  pretty interesting nonetheless  concluding our list we have the el  tannen antenna a mysterious object  photographed on the ocean floor in the  1960s  antarctic research ship the usnsl tannen  is the vessel which captured the strange  antenna-like artifact on camera  the ship was traveling west of cape horn  in south america when crew members  spotted the object at a strikingly deep  depth of over  3 900 meters or 12  800 feet below the ocean's surface in a  region close to total darkness  so what was this alien-looking object so  far below sea level  probably a type of sea sponge  chondrocladia concrens is a species of  carnivorous sponge with unusual  appendages which  vaguely resemble an antenna and is  almost certainly what the crew  photographed  a pretty wild organism even if it's not  quite as astounding as some deep-sea  radio dish  and that's the end of our analysis of  seven interesting out of place artifacts  and the explanations behind them  i hope you had fun and perhaps learn  something new along the way  if you did please consider subscribing  to curious archive  and leaving this video alike thank you  so much and i'll see you in the next  video  [Music]  you

